REGENT OF BANGKA,

Considering : a. that the empowerment of women is carried out so that women can actualize their potential optimally to participate in development in accordance with their nature and capacity;

b. that women as national assets who play a role in the process of continuation and preparation of quality generations, need to receive guarantees of their rights and protection from acts of violence and discrimination in order to build society, nation and state;

c. that based on the provisions of Article 12 paragraph (2) letter b of Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government, mandates that women's empowerment is a mandatory affair organized by the Regency Regional Government;

d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Implementation of Women's Empowerment and Protection;

In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 28 of 1959 concerning the Stipulation of Emergency Law Number 4 of 1956 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1956 Number 55) Emergency Law Number 5 of 1956 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1956 Number 56) and Emergency Law Number 6 of 1956 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1956 Number 57) concerning the Establishment of Level II Regions including Kotaparaja Within the Level I Region of South Sumatra As Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1959 Number 73, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 1821);

3. Law Number 27 of 2000 concerning the Establishment of Bangka Belitung Islands Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 217, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia 4033);

4. Law Number 1 of 1974 concerning Marriage (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1945 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1974 Number 1, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3019);

5. Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on The Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1984 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3277);

